Respond with JSON only, no other text, matching exactly one of these three shapes:

CONSULT — ask the repository consultant evidence-backed questions:
{"action":"CONSULT","reason":"why more evidence is needed","repo":"orders-service","questions":["Where is X implemented and what test file should prove it?"],"paths":["src/x.ts"],"tasks":[]}

FINALIZE — propose the final task breakdown (only after at least one successful consultation):
{"action":"FINALIZE","reason":"evidence is sufficient for every task","questions":[],"paths":[],"tasks":[{"id":"T1","title":"...","description":"...","area":"...","repo":"orders-service","scenario":"...","touches":["src/x.ts"],"testPath":"test/x.test.ts","blockedBy":[]}]}

BLOCKED — stop; a real prerequisite is missing (contradictory evidence, unanswerable scope):
{"action":"BLOCKED","reason":"the specific missing prerequisite","questions":[],"paths":[],"tasks":[]}

Field rules:
- reason: always required, nonblank, explains the decision.
- CONSULT repo: required, the single repo the consultant inspects this round; touches/testPath
  catalog entries are per repo. questions: 1-8 nonblank repository questions asking for concrete
  file/symbol-level evidence, not general design opinions. paths: repo-relative files/tests you
  want the consultant to check for existence (may be empty).
- FINALIZE tasks: exactly one task per scenario listed above, no unknown scenario.
  id: T1, T2, ... in dependency order.
  title: at most 70 characters, an imperative slug naming the behavior; no "Implement"/"Task"
  prefix, no quotation marks, not the scenario name copied verbatim.
  description: markdown, naming the approach/functions/modules found in the consultation evidence
  and exactly what the test must assert.
  area: one of the areas listed above; must be one the task's repo serves.
  repo: one of the repo ids listed above; area must be one that repo serves.
  touches: 1-8 repo-relative files the build agent may edit — every touches/testPath value MUST
  already appear in the consultation file catalog above; a path the consultant never checked
  cannot be used here — request it in an earlier CONSULT round instead.
  testPath: the single test file that proves the scenario.
  blockedBy: ids of earlier tasks (by this same breakdown) that must land first.
- BLOCKED: reason must name the specific missing prerequisite — never used to silently approve
  incomplete coverage or to paper over contradictory evidence.
Never fabricate a file path, function name, or existence claim — only what the consultation
evidence above actually supports.
